# Connect VS Code

Connect GitHub Copilot in [VS Code](https://code.visualstudio.com) to Colliedesk. VS Code asks for
the token once and stores it securely; it never appears in the configuration file.

{{template "before" .}}
## Connect

1. In VS Code, run **MCP: Open User Configuration** from the Command Palette.
2. Add the `inputs` entry and the `{{.ServerName}}` server below to the file (keep what is already
   in it):

   ```json
   {{indent 3 (index .Snippets "vscode")}}
   ```

3. Start the server from the file or the **MCP Servers** view. VS Code asks for the Colliedesk
   agent token once: paste it.

The `{{.ServerName}}` tools then show in the tools picker of Copilot chat in agent mode.

{{template "try" .}}
{{template "tiers" .}}
## Remove it

Delete the `{{.ServerName}}` server and the `colliedesk-token` input from the file. {{template "revoke" .}}
